cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite both the manuscript and this archived release."
title: "Independent external validation of virtual multiplex immunofluorescence from H&E reveals that predicted channels encode tissue composition rather than cell identity"
abstract: >-
  Code and derived results for an independent external validation of GigaTIME and GigaTIME-Flash. We
  reproduced the authors' own released evaluation protocol, then tested both models against four independently
  generated real-measurement datasets spanning pixel, spatial-transcriptomic, patient and single-cell
  resolution. Virtual mIF supports tissue-composition characterisation but not quantitative marker readout.
